      "writtenOn": "2010-10-04T19:11:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Haven\u0027t thoroughly reviewed spec, but this doesn\u0027t make sense to me:  EF_CPHS_ONS[_SHORT] is the name of the operator who issued the SIM (ie, CPHS version of SPN).  Why would we display this for EONS, which should be the name of the operator for the currently registered network?  If roaming, these can be completely different operators.",
      "revId": "fff5d2bdddc337e0343b8daba8c8a6c1c79be319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAA73///x0\u003d",
