      "writtenOn": "2010-10-04T19:11:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem quite right.  If this were a private method called only in pollStateDone(), it would be fine.  But it can also be called from GsmPhone in response to EVENT_ICC_RECORDS_EONS_UPDATED.  My two issues with that:  1) Seems a bit circular (SimRecords -\u003e GsmPhone -\u003e GsmSST -\u003e SimRecords); and 2) In that code path, ss is updated but phone.notifyServiceStateChanged() is not called, so no apps are notified of the operator name change.",
      "revId": "fff5d2bdddc337e0343b8daba8c8a6c1c79be319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAA73///xE\u003d",
        "filename": "telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GsmServiceStateTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 584,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2010-10-05T08:57:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Issue1: This is circular because when there is a OTA refresh of OPL/PNN files, EONS name is to be derived (this can be triggered in SIMRecords itself). This derived name has to be updated in SS and also this name has to be updated in the display. For both these things we need phone object again. This is again done to avoid dependency on phone object .\nIssue2: This is definitely an issue. This can be fixed by moving the phone.notifyServiceStateChanged() to updateEons() if you agree.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAA73///4s\u003d",
      "revId": "fff5d2bdddc337e0343b8daba8c8a6c1c79be319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
